Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca8084: do not advertise EEE by default

The qca808x driver has no EEE ops, so phylib keeps whatever EEE
advertisement the PHY has out of reset and replays it at every
auto-negotiation. On the QCA8084 that reset default is "advertise
everything". With some link partners this trains badly: ISP ONTs
(Eltex, Huawei) at 1G show a storm of rx CRC errors, QUIC/UDP loss
and link flaps until EEE is switched off. The PPE MAC cannot signal
LPI anyway, so EEE buys nothing here.

Clear the advertisement and the enabled flag in config_init. phylib
then writes zero EEE advertisement at every aneg. Users who want EEE
can still turn it on with ethtool --set-eee, the eee_disabled_modes
mask is left untouched.

Signed-off-by: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -944,6 +944,17 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/* phylib preserves the EEE advertisement found at probe, and
+	 * this PHY advertises EEE out of reset. EEE trains badly with
+	 * some link partners (ISP ONTs at 1G were reported with rx CRC
+	 * errors and link flaps), and the MAC cannot signal LPI, so do
+	 * not advertise it by default. ethtool --set-eee can still turn
+	 * it on.
+	 */
+	linkmode_zero(phydev->advertising_eee);
+	phydev->eee_cfg.eee_enabled = false;
+	phydev->eee_cfg.tx_lpi_enabled = false;
+
 	if (phy_package_init_once(phydev)) {
 		ret = qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once(phydev);
 		if (ret)
